Patches applied to the pristine util-linux-2.42.4 tarball by ../unpack.sh.

They apply with `patch -p1` from inside src/, in filename order.  Each one
starts with a few lines of prose saying what it does and why, then the diff.

  0001-platform-block-headers.patch
        The BLKPG partition interface and the discard/zero-out requests are
        declared in <sys/mount.h> here, with the other BLK* requests.

  0002-no-o-path-o-direct.patch
        No O_PATH descriptors and no direct I/O: the symlink-free open
        helper reports its verification as unavailable, the loop device
        code opens backing files for ordinary I/O.

  0003-terminal-no-echoprt.patch
        The terminal has no ECHOPRT mode; the terminal reset helper clears
        nothing for it.

